{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"maize-wintery-larva","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nGerrit Verify run 31892203411 completed in 31m59s; macOS remained the critical path, with the default pytest step taking 1,545.29s and integration 155.01s. The workflow runs the same default selector in Ubuntu 3.11/3.12/3.13 and macOS 3.13 even for tests whose only input is the immutable checked-out repository tree. A node-level audit found 19 repository-policy/AST cases across seven mixed test modules. They passed locally under three workers in 8.28s. Moving whole files or general behavioral tests would weaken macOS platform coverage; adding a new Ubuntu shard would duplicate checkout, install, collection, and session fixtures and consume another contentious runner. Five surveyed active OSS projects (pytest, pip, Pydantic, Click, uv) keep behavioral suites on macOS and run static/lint checks on Linux. Internal precedents feathered-ironclad-macaque and isleless-catatonic-ekaltadeta accept singleton routing; ropeable-hydrated-siskin and coercive-paediatric-bug reject reduced macOS behavioral coverage and extra runner sharding.\n\n## Plan\n- Register a strict `repo_policy` pytest marker for tests whose complete contract is an OS/Python-invariant scan of repository text or AST.\n- Mark only the 19 proven tree-policy nodes, not whole mixed modules; retain runtime, subprocess, filesystem, locking, timeout, and Git behavior in all four cells.\n- Keep the marked nodes in the existing Ubuntu 3.13 default-suite process and exclude them only from Ubuntu 3.11, Ubuntu 3.12, and macOS 3.13. Add no job, runner, checkout, install, collection session, or fixture setup.\n- Add a workflow contract oracle that collects the real selectors, proves marked cases execute exactly once, proves unmarked cases in the mixed modules retain four-cell coverage, pins the primary cell, and proves integration routing is unchanged.\n- Preserve the coverage report on Ubuntu 3.13 and every existing default/integration matrix cell.\n- Run focused tests, workflow parity, lint, typecheck, and the complete non-external suite. Measure the next organic Gerrit run rather than creating a control patch solely for timing. Back out with a Gerrit revert if collection multiplicity or platform coverage regresses.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Exactly 19 proven OS/Python-invariant repository-policy cases carry the strict marker.\n- [ ] Every marked assertion executes once per full code-change CI run in Ubuntu 3.13.\n- [ ] Marked cases are excluded only from Ubuntu 3.11, Ubuntu 3.12, and macOS 3.13.\n- [ ] Every unmarked default-tier test retains its prior four-cell matrix coverage.\n- [ ] Runtime/subprocess tests in the seven mixed modules remain unmarked and retain macOS coverage.\n- [ ] Integration selection and all four default/integration matrix cells remain present.\n- [ ] No new job, runner, checkout, dependency install, pytest collection session, or fixture session is added.\n- [ ] OSS and tracker precedent is recorded and meets the standing consensus approval rule.\n- [ ] Focused tests, workflow parity tests, lint, typecheck, and complete non-external suite pass.\n- [ ] Gerrit receives LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 before merge.\n- [ ] The first organic post-merge full-route run records macOS and aggregate runner-time deltas.","id":"abb9-1652-8840-4640","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":["ci","performance","macos","tests"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Run repository-policy pytest guards once on Ubuntu 3.13"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786814491959878001,"uuid":"ce173184-d53d-46c9-a5e1-d76e2c97fc98"}